{"text":"This would lead to a take-off in global economic growth, rebounding Europe, and rebounding Asia, both of whom have been catalyzing forces behind Africa's own recent progress. When President John F. Kennedy, another Harvard graduate, spoke to this audience in 1956, as a junior senator from Massachusetts, he pointed to two keystones for progress, nameless scholarly objectivity and technological capability. He said, we need both the technical judgment and the disinterested viewpoint of the scholar to prevent us from becoming imprisoned by our own slogans. In newly democratic societies where battles are marked with distinctive icons as well as names, since many fortress remain illiterate, the danger for sloganeering political populism is only greater and can lead down the road of war, not just bad policy choices.","words":[{"text":"This","start":0.0,"end":0.84},{"text":"would","start":0.84,"end":1.06},{"text":"lead","start":1.06,"end":1.3},{"text":"to","start":1.3,"end":1.52},{"text":"a","start":1.52,"end":1.62},{"text":"take-off","start":1.62,"end":2.12},{"text":"in","start":2.12,"end":2.9},{"text":"global","start":2.9,"end":3.22},{"text":"economic","start":3.22,"end":3.82},{"text":"growth","start":3.82,"end":4.34,"punct":","},{"text":"rebounding","start":5.18,"end":5.72},{"text":"Europe","start":5.72,"end":6.26,"punct":","},{"text":"and","start":7.58,"end":7.86},{"text":"rebounding","start":7.86,"end":8.74},{"text":"Asia","start":8.74,"end":9.3,"punct":","},{"text":"both","start":9.9,"end":10.14},{"text":"of","start":10.14,"end":10.34},{"text":"whom","start":10.34,"end":10.56},{"text":"have","start":10.56,"end":10.76},{"text":"been","start":10.76,"end":10.98},{"text":"catalyzing","start":10.98,"end":11.68},{"text":"forces","start":11.68,"end":12.18},{"text":"behind","start":12.18,"end":12.68},{"text":"Africa's","start":12.68,"end":13.3},{"text":"own","start":13.3,"end":13.56},{"text":"recent","start":13.56,"end":13.86},{"text":"progress","start":13.86,"end":1